# HakiOS fragment: the Qualcomm SM8450 family (SM8450, SM8475: "waipio", "cape") -- what is true of the SoC, whatever device it is in.
# Eight cores in MPIDR's second affinity field: 0-3 Cortex-A510, 4-6 Cortex-A710, 7 Cortex-X2. The interrupt controller is a
# GIC-600 with GICv4 frames (0x17100000, redistributors at 0x17180000, 0x40000 apart), which the loader's platform describes.
#
# None of the SoC drivers is turned on yet: cpufreq, thermal, socinfo and the PMIC arbiter were written against SC7280's
# addresses (the kernel's defaults), and on this family each of them has to be checked against the device tree first
# (docs/porting/index.md, step 3). Until then the kernel runs on one core, the one the loader hands it.
CONFIG_SOC="sm8450"
CONFIG_CPUS=1
